<p>Venezuela’s National Assembly says it has received more than 1,500 requests for amnesty from people described as political prisoners, after a new amnesty law took effect this week. Authorities say hundreds of people have already received amnesty under the law. Supporters describe the measure as a step toward easing political tensions and reuniting families. The next question is how quickly officials work through the remaining requests — and what standards they use to decide who qualifies.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/493Tkbr4lSFMX8rjhXbROs0BxpE6aNtsZSHjjEOnfGuXaHqbvcTwih47FDVZPOrm7TUGjxwWuMeccEnWjTxCLsq_-dzRHkkLvuxQjCh8-FgO9iohj1o0RP7CCDIpnCbhN4bammfdDIBHJNP4SQQ8y9TvJuTpaaWX2GawGMO2MMSuoQ3Lv1tWaA1_ZgF9q16ym2xiDI3AQGc1Jx697QIqlGpa-QoA7v-iYdf1xcxCd7Y702Zu56URYq7bltsERwJAyk4Be6LSNvBVxvvA9QA' alt='Venezuela’s National Assembly during deliberations on the amnesty law.' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Requests volume: National Assembly President Jorge Rodríguez said on state-run television that authorities have received more than 1,550 applications under the new law.</li><li>Legislative backing: The Hindu notes the law passed unanimously in the National Assembly, a rare show of unity.</li><li>Initial grants: The Hindu says 379 people received amnesty soon after the law was adopted, pointing to rapid early implementation.</li><li>Timing: Firstpost reports the surge in applications was disclosed two days after the measure took effect.</li></ul><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>National Assembly leadership (Jorge Rodríguez): On state-run television, he described the rollout as an active intake-and-review process that is still underway. (<a href='https://www.straitstimes.com/world/venezuela-has-received-more-than-1550-requests-under-amnesty-law'>The Straits Times</a>)</li><li>Venezuela’s National Assembly (institution): Coverage depicts the legislature presenting the law as a formal path to resolve politically linked cases and free people described as political prisoners. (<a href='https://www.thehindu.com/news/international/venezuela-grants-amnesty-to-379-political-prisoners/article70661066.ece'>The Hindu</a>)</li><li>United States (as described by outlets): Some coverage frames the legislation as US-backed or passed under pressure from Washington; the BBC ties that pressure to events after the capture of ex-President Nicolás Maduro. (<a href='https://www.aljazeera.com/news/2026/2/21/venezuela-receives-more-than-1500-amnesty-requests-under-new-law'>Al Jazeera</a>, <a href='https://www.firstpost.com/world/over-1500-political-prisoners-in-venezuela-request-amnesty-under-new-law-13982343.html'>Firstpost</a>, <a href='https://www.bbc.com/news/articles/c93w9g2dvn5o'>BBC</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://www.firstpost.com/world/over-1500-political-prisoners-in-venezuela-request-amnesty-under-new-law-13982343.html'>Over 1,500 political prisoners in Venezuela request amnesty under new law</a> - firstpost.com</li><li><a href='https://www.thehindu.com/news/international/venezuela-grants-amnesty-to-379-political-prisoners/article70661066.ece'>Venezuela grants amnesty to 379 political prisoners</a> - thehindu.com</li><li><a href='https://www.aljazeera.com/news/2026/2/21/venezuela-receives-more-than-1500-amnesty-requests-under-new-law'>Venezuela receives more than 1,500 amnesty requests under new law</a> - aljazeera.com</li><li><a href='https://www.bbc.com/news/articles/c93w9g2dvn5o'>More than 1,500 Venezuelan political prisoners apply for amnesty</a> - bbc.com</li><li><a href='https://www.straitstimes.com/world/venezuela-has-received-more-than-1550-requests-under-amnesty-law'>Venezuela has received more than 1,550 requests under amnesty law</a> - straitstimes.com</li></ul>